# .gitignore of a framing repository.
#
# This repository holds ONLY framing documents: no code, no build artefact. The list is therefore
# short, and that is normal. Every entry says why it is here — a folder's name decides nothing,
# only this file does.
#
# ⚠ PRIVATE repository. A workshop's framing is never published: it carries names, decisions and
# session context belonging to its owner.

# ── Editor tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Machine-local settings, and the editor workspace file, which lives at the corpus root and
# belongs to no repository.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# ── Temporary files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors drop working copies beside the file being edited; they appear and vanish as you type.
~$*
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~

# ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Local, unshared work ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drafts, exports, throwaway notes. The folder exists so there is somewhere to put a file without
# wondering whether it should be versioned: by construction, the answer is no.
_local/
